I do not even know where to start. Three orders, three problems, and every
time I contact support I get a different person asking me to explain
everything again from the beginning.

Order AUR-20410 was supposed to be a black standing desk. What arrived was the
white compact model, which does not fit the space at all and is not what I
paid for. I reported it immediately. That was eleven days ago. I was told a
return label would be sent "within 24 hours". No label has ever arrived. My
emails get answers like "we are escalating this" and then nothing happens for
days. Follow-up number two and number three produced the same reply, word for
word, from different people.

The desk problem has also cost me money, not just time. I work from home and
had nowhere to put my monitor, so I bought a temporary desk from a local shop
that I would never have needed if the correct item had arrived. I have now
spent close to four hours on your phone line across two weeks, including one
call where I was on hold for forty-five minutes and then disconnected while
being transferred to a supervisor who, as far as I can tell, does not exist.

Then there is the double billing. Order AUR-20455 (monitor arm) was charged to
my card twice, 149 dollars each time. I called my bank and they said the
merchant has to release the duplicate; your support told me it was "passed to
the billing team" and after that I heard nothing again. That was two weeks
ago. I have started keeping a written log of every interaction, with dates,
reference numbers and the name of whoever I spoke to, because I cannot keep
reconstructing this story from memory for each new agent.

And then there is Ryan. On my third call about the desk, Ryan told me the
issue "was probably my fault for ordering the wrong item" which is simply not
true - the invoice itself shows the compact model at the compact price, but I
paid the price of the full-size desk. He then said he would "check with the
warehouse" and hung up. I have the chat transcript.

On top of all of this, order AUR-20488 (the lamp) arrived four days late, which
by itself I would not even mention in a normal week. The box was crushed and
the lampshade has a dent, which I photographed at the time.

I want three things, and I want them in writing from one person: the correct
desk or my money back, the duplicate charge reversed, and a named senior
human being to take ownership of this whole mess instead of passing me around
a queue. I am not angry at any individual - I am angry at a process that
clearly does not work, and I am documenting all of it now. If nothing moves
this week I will be taking the billing issue to my bank and the rest to the
consumer forum, which is not how I want to spend my time.

